  "prompt": "(tokenizer)Snowflake: comment markers inside unquoted stage paths are tokenized as comments\n\n**Fully reproducible code snippet**\n\nWith `read=\"snowflake\"`, `--`, `//` and `/*` inside an unquoted stage path or `file://` URI are tokenized as comment starts, so the path gets truncated or tokenization fails:\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\n\nparse_one(\"select $1 from @s/a--b\", read=\"snowflake\").sql(\"snowflake\")\n# actual:   'SELECT $1 FROM @s/a /* b */'\n# expected: 'SELECT $1 FROM @s/a--b'\n\nparse_one(\"select $1 from @s/a//b\", read=\"snowflake\").sql(\"snowflake\")\n# actual:   'SELECT $1 FROM @s/a /* b */'\n# expected: 'SELECT $1 FROM @s/a//b'\n\nparse_one(\"select $1 from @s/a/*b\", read=\"snowflake\")\n# actual:   TokenError\n# expected: 'SELECT $1 FROM @s/a/*b'\n\nparse_one(\"copy into t from @s/a--b/c\", read=\"snowflake\").sql(\"snowflake\")\n# actual:   'COPY INTO t FROM @s/a /* b/c */'\n# expected: 'COPY INTO t FROM @s/a--b/c'\n\nparse_one(\"put file:///tmp/a--b @s/p\", read=\"snowflake\").sql(\"snowflake\")\n# actual:   \"PUT 'file:///tmp/a' put file:///tmp/a /* b @s/p */\"\n# expected: \"PUT 'file:///tmp/a--b' @s/p\"\n```\n\n`LIST @s/a--b` has the same problem. Quoted paths such as `'@s/a--b'` are handled correctly.\n\nThis is easy to miss because `@s/a--b` and `@s/a--c` parse to the same statement, so regenerated SQL silently reads from a different location.\n\nReproduced on main (83622a530).\n\n**Snowflake behavior**\n\nThe docs don't spell out where an unquoted path ends, so I checked against a live account by unloading files to unquoted paths and listing them:\n\n- `copy into @stg/a--b/ from (select 1)` writes to `a--b/`, and `select $1 from @stg/a--b/c` reads only that prefix. `//`, `/*`, `*/`, `#`, `=` and `\"` inside the path behave the same way.\n- The path ends at whitespace or at one of ``, ; ( ) ' ` ~ < > |``. The exception is `~` right after `@`, since `@~` is the user stage.\n- A comment after whitespace is still a comment: `select $1 from @stg/a -- note` works as expected.\n- The same rules apply to `file://` URIs in `PUT`: `put file:///dir/a--b.csv @stg` uploads `a--b.csv`.\n\n**Official Documentation**\n\n- https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/querying-stage\n- https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/list\n- https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/copy-into-table\n- https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/put",
